<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Developers · Kurukoo</title><meta name="description" content="Build on Kurukoo's conversation, capability, network and execution surfaces with governed APIs and integrations."><link rel="icon" href="/assets/brand/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site.css?v=1.2.1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/kurukoo-public-pages.css?v=3"></head><body><main class="k-public-page"><header class="k-public-page-header"><a href="/" class="k-public-brand">Kurukoo</a><nav><a href="/features">Features</a><a href="/network">Network</a><a href="/developers/api">API</a><a href="/chat">Ask Kurukoo</a></nav></header><section class="k-public-hero"><span class="k-eyebrow">Developers</span><h1>Build around a conversation-first operating system.</h1><p>Kurukoo exposes governed capabilities through canonical conversation, identity, request, provider, agent, connection and evidence boundaries.</p><a class="k-button-primary" href="/developers/api">Explore the API</a></section><section class="k-public-section"><h2>Build around durable product objects</h2><div class="k-public-grid"><article><h3>Conversations</h3><p>Create contextual experiences that hand users back to Agent without creating a second conversational identity.</p></article><article><h3>Requests</h3><p>Represent user objectives as durable requests with explicit lifecycle, authorization and evidence.</p></article><article><h3>Capabilities</h3><p>Discover and compose Kurukoo capabilities without bypassing policy or truth boundaries.</p></article><article><h3>Connections</h3><p>Connect channels, devices and external services through one owner-scoped relationship.</p></article></div></section><section class="k-public-section"><h2>Governance is part of the platform</h2><p>API consumers do not receive a shortcut around authentication, consent, payment, provider verification, execution authorization or evidence. Kurukoo keeps those boundaries canonical so integrations can remain powerful without becoming unsafe or misleading.</p><a class="k-text-link" href="/developers/api">Read API guidance →</a></section></main></body></html>
